          %h2#ugly_display_of_pre_blocks Ugly display of “pre” blocks
          %p
            (I had to take wraping pre in
            %code &lt;code;&gt;
            to get title acceptible)
          %p
            Display of
            %code &lt;pre&gt;
            is rather ugly with all the extra white space. It really needs some CSS styling.
          %p
            (LETS SEE If I can directly put in a
            %code &lt;style&gt;
            block and change it)
          \&lt;style&gt;pre { white-space: pre-wrap; border-left-width-value: 6px;  border-left-style-value: solid; border-left-color-value: rgb(200, 200, 170); padding-top: 8px; padding-right-value: 8px; padding-bottom: 8px; padding-left-value: 16px; background-color: rgb(235, 236, 255); margin-top: 1em; margin-right-value: 0pt; margin-bottom: 1em; margin-left-value: 0pt;}&lt;/style&gt;
          %p (ANY BETTER?)
          %pre
            :preserve
              o = {a: 1,
                   b: 2
                  }          %p
            The
            %a{:href => "http://golem.ph.utexas.edu/wiki/instiki/show/Syntax#SyntaxColouring"} Javascript syntax coloring
            is the same but only colored. (I recall that I had to put in a “The” at the start of this pgh so I wouldn’t get a parse error.)
          %pre.javascript
            %code.javascript
              %span.ident o
              %span.other =
              %span.other {
              %span.ident a
              %span.other :
              %span.integer 1
              %span.other ,
              %span.ident b
              %span.other :
              %span.integer 2
              %span.other }
